cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "LeanDring: a Lean 4 formalization of the monomial representation ring and of species-table rigidity"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 + Mathlib formalization of the monomial representation ring D(G)
  (the complex-fibered Burnside ring), of species-table rigidity for groups of
  order p^4, and of the order-5^5 counterexample to D-ring rigidity: the
  unconditional, kernel-checked theorem
  Nonempty (DRing (Coordinate 1) ≃+* DRing (Coordinate 2)),
  i.e. the two groups of order 5^5 labelled SmallGroup(3125,68) and
  SmallGroup(3125,69) by GAP have isomorphic D-rings. Everything compiled by
  lake build is sorry-free and uses no custom axioms and no native_decide; the
  declarations cited by the accompanying paper are collected in
  LeanDring/MainResults.lean.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vassias
    given-names: Tilemachos
    email: tilemachos.vassias@gmail.com
license: Apache-2.0
